{"data":[{"author_id":"1889503910437724161","created_at":"2026-10-28T22:22:46.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2115569991474885114"],"id":"2115569991474885114","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":11,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Cancelled my X Premium. Grok Build usage limits have been severely lowered, and Muse gives me an always-on agent VM, and lets me code for FREE with much higher limits. X is still a great platform, though. I would come back to X Premium if they included Grok Bot and gave a lot","url":"https://x.com/Damien_Ducate/status/2115569991474885114"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2115556523573178368"]},"author_id":"3075199947","created_at":"2026-10-28T21:30:10.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2115556754725478486"],"id":"2115556754725478486","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":23,"impression_count":914,"like_count":18,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":12,"retweet_count":1},"referenced_tweets":[{"id":"2115131580264149313","type":"quoted"}],"text":"The head of OpenAI’s Codex just published his entire personal AI assistant setup.\n\nAlexander Embiricos runs two assistants. One is a person. The other is dots, OpenAI’s always-on agent inside ChatGPT.\n\nHere’s how it’s set up:\n\n1. Every dot gets its own cloud computer and browser, https://t.co/fQgIpDajnR https://t.co/lQH1SFNmdr","url":"https://x.com/undefinedKi/status/2115556754725478486"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["7_2115533519053078529"]},"author_id":"1712518601117200384","created_at":"2026-10-28T19:57:52.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2115533530298040616"],"id":"2115533530298040616","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":3,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":0},"text":"ChatGPT's dots now live in your texts. US Pro users (preview) can hand their always-on agent a task over iMessage or RCS, with photos or voice notes, and it pings back with updates.\n\nFine print worth reading: texts route through a third party, Linq, so they're not end-to-end https://t.co/VKxmSoC7GD","url":"https://x.com/DarceX26/status/2115533530298040616"},{"author_id":"539964056","created_at":"2026-10-28T19:43:55.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2115530016402612383"],"id":"2115530016402612383","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":24,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":0},"text":"People, if you’re not using an always-on agent (OpenClaw, Hermes, Grok Bot, Muse, Duet, or anything else), you’re missing out!\n\nWhether it’s job searching, content creation, productivity, or 100 other things, it’s a massive lifestyle boost!\n\nTry it. You won’t regret it!","url":"https://x.com/suresh42326/status/2115530016402612383"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["13_2115494759447904257"]},"author_id":"2096819916175212548","created_at":"2026-10-28T18:35:21.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2115512763749446117"],"id":"2115512763749446117","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":1,"impression_count":962,"like_count":11,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":0},"text":"ChatGPT announces texting for dots, its always-on agent\n\n&gt; Text your dot over iMessage or RCS with words, photos or voice notes, and it texts you first when something needs you\n &gt; Only you can text it, and it can't see your other texts\n &gt; Beta for ChatGPT Pro users in the US,","url":"https://x.com/alexmichael/status/2115512763749446117"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2115509220795686912"]},"author_id":"853318060052291584","created_at":"2026-10-28T18:21:18.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2115509226709676448"],"id":"2115509226709676448","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":1580,"like_count":7,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":4,"retweet_count":0},"text":"NVIDIA Takes $3B Meta Equity Stake, Turning Biggest Customer Into Strategic Partner | Kyle Belmonte, Techtimes\n\nNVIDIA committed $3 billion to Meta's equity offering on Monday, converting the world's dominant AI chip supplier into a financial stakeholder in the social media https://t.co/VuPegOdkaS","url":"https://x.com/OwenGregorian/status/2115509226709676448"},{"author_id":"1543232005940383748","created_at":"2026-10-28T16:14:51.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2115477402507977080"],"id":"2115477402507977080","in_reply_to_user_id":"1573399256836309009","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":76,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"referenced_tweets":[{"id":"2115470152598946259","type":"replied_to"}],"text":"@kimmonismus @Meta Europe getting an always-on agent on launch day instead of six months later. Progress. Now imagine EU regulators moving at agent speed too. By the time the guidance lands, Dots will have filed most of the paperwork itself.","url":"https://x.com/JHighmo/status/2115477402507977080"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["7_2115474370915172352"]},"author_id":"1722607238","created_at":"2026-10-28T16:03:11.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2115474467405135928"],"id":"2115474467405135928","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":25,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Claude Duet is Anthropic's always-on agent: it works while you're away, in one thread, and it's Claude-only, unlike Grok Bot.\n\nResearch preview. US Pro and Max waitlist; it asks approval before sending, paying or deleting.\n\nComment DUET for the link. #ClaudeAI https://t.co/t0gborFMb5","url":"https://x.com/FarhanRakhangi/status/2115474467405135928"},{"author_id":"2110381643693453312","created_at":"2026-10-28T15:50:00.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2115471150239096916"],"id":"2115471150239096916","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":1,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Grok Bot (and any always-on agent) is more useful when you treat it as a teammate that owns a result, not a chatbot that owns a conversation.\n\nThe open-source pieces that make this practical:\n\n- Official Grok Build harness (agent loop, tools, TUI, skills, MCP):","url":"https://x.com/maiboltahun/status/2115471150239096916"},{"author_id":"2097678785550135297","created_at":"2026-10-28T15:48:16.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2115470713763373469"],"id":"2115470713763373469","in_reply_to_user_id":"1573399256836309009","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":6,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"referenced_tweets":[{"id":"2115470152598946259","type":"replied_to"}],"text":"@kimmonismus @Meta Business and enterprise first makes sense for an always-on agent, since admins can set the guardrails. Curious what Dots is actually allowed to touch in the EU version, given the AI Act rules on automated decisions.","url":"https://x.com/ChatisRetoro/status/2115470713763373469"},{"author_id":"1573399256836309009","created_at":"2026-10-28T15:46:02.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2115470152598946259"],"id":"2115470152598946259","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":20,"impression_count":19033,"like_count":348,"quote_count":4,"reply_count":61,"retweet_count":7},"referenced_tweets":[{"id":"2115450637521666055","type":"quoted"}],"text":"OpenAIs always-on-agent \"Dots\" will be available in the EU today for business and enterprise.\n\nConsumer plans soon. Hope Meta Muse follows soon as well, @Meta https://t.co/dZD35baHAH","url":"https://x.com/kimmonismus/status/2115470152598946259"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2115428609913479168"]},"author_id":"1993577742659678209","created_at":"2026-10-28T13:00:58.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2115428612367089790"],"id":"2115428612367089790","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":2,"like_count":1,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"OpenAI DevDay 2026 in one list: Dots (always-on agent), Codex in Cloud, Plugins, ChatGPT Spaces, apps via subscription, and GPT-6.1.\n\nWhich one matters most to you?\n\nHinglish breakdown 👇\nhttps://t.co/XtC8VZzuZg\nhttps://t.co/9SuUzc3PIE https://t.co/WHqGrapZ3d","url":"https://x.com/mohitmandawat01/status/2115428612367089790"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2115414612598235136"]},"author_id":"1018196615289561089","created_at":"2026-10-28T12:10:56.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2115414615068696697","2115416019204465002"],"id":"2115416019204465002","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":25,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"In 10 weeks, 4 AI labs shipped personal agents that never log off.\nMost researchers will hand them the wrong jobs.\n\nThis month I finished my April travel reimbursements.\n6 months late.\n\nFederally funded PIs spend an estimated 44% of research time on admin.\nChatGPT cleared my pile https://t.co/bxVyhNhC1H","url":"https://x.com/paraskarmachary/status/2115416019204465002"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2115414612598235136"]},"author_id":"1018196615289561089","created_at":"2026-10-28T12:05:21.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2115414615068696697","2115416019204465002"],"id":"2115414615068696697","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":9,"like_count":1,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"In 10 weeks, 4 AI labs shipped personal agents that never log off.\nMost researchers will hand them the wrong jobs.\n\nThis month I finished my April travel reimbursements.\n6 months late.\n\nFederally funded PIs spend an estimated 44% of research time on admin.\nChatGPT cleared my pile https://t.co/Uc7boCcnVD","url":"https://x.com/paraskarmachary/status/2115414615068696697"},{"article":{"title":"Another Daily AI Newsletter - October 28"},"author_id":"1941681257630531588","created_at":"2026-10-28T12:03:02.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2115414032920494229"],"id":"2115414032920494229","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":1471,"like_count":5,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":1},"text":"An internal Claude model chained exploits across Chrome, Safari, Android, Windows and Linux, DeepMind introduced Genie 4, OpenAI confidentially filed a draft S-1 and launched CodexMax, and SK Hynix posted a record quarter on AI memory. Another day in AI. https://t.co/etqfPJ6vPW","url":"https://x.com/AnotherCodingX/status/2115414032920494229"}],"includes":{"media":[{"media_key":"3_2115556523573178368","type":"photo","url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVv3cxHW8AAmJlM.png"},{"media_key":"7_2115533519053078529","preview_image_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/2115533519053078529/pu/img/ExYyiEblc0zUryPb.jpg","type":"video"},{"media_key":"13_2115494759447904257","preview_image_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2115494759447904257/img/gnlEjizTFyuOlfML.jpg","type":"video"},{"media_key":"3_2115509220795686912","type":"photo","url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVvMbYiXIAA3Vxg.jpg"},{"media_key":"7_2115474370915172352","preview_image_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/2115474370915172352/pu/img/eP9oruLw4Xq_5RAD.jpg","type":"video"},{"media_key":"3_2115428609913479168","type":"photo","url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVuDHNmXYAAcA--.jpg"},{"media_key":"3_2115414612598235136","type":"photo","url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVt2YdiWoAArGIg.jpg"}],"users":[{"id":"1889503910437724161","name":"Damien","profile_image_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1889506687079555075/weO15VhY_normal.jpg","username":"Damien_Ducate","verified":false},{"id":"3075199947","name":"Yarchi","profile_image_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2054664188417413120/DZKz0Tqn_normal.jpg","username":"undefinedKi","verified":false},{"id":"1712518601117200384","name":"Darce","profile_image_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2039071067369791488/AYSN9GCw_normal.jpg","username":"DarceX26","verified":false},{"id":"539964056","name":"చలం","profile_image_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1306844551030607874/HA8Z4M_5_normal.jpg","username":"suresh42326","verified":false},{"id":"2096819916175212548","